<div class="bg-zinc-950 text-zinc-100">
  <.marketing_nav current_user={@current_user} current={:docs} />

  <section class="py-12 sm:py-16">
    <.docs_layout
      current="integrations-entra"
      updated="August 25, 2026"
      evidence="Live-tested against a Microsoft Entra tenant on August 25, 2026."
      toc={[
        {"sso", "Single sign-on"},
        {"scim", "Directory sync"}
      ]}
    >
      <.docs_header current="integrations-entra">
        <:dek>
          Connect Microsoft Entra to emisar: an app registration signs people in with the oid claim,
          and a separate enterprise application provisions the directory.
        </:dek>
      </.docs_header>
      <.docs_prerequisites>
        <:item>An <strong class="text-zinc-300">Entra administrator</strong>.</:item>
        <:item>An emisar <strong class="text-zinc-300">owner or admin</strong>.</:item>
      </.docs_prerequisites>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        The sections below build two objects in order — sign-in first, then the directory.
      </p>

      <.docs_h2 id="sso">Single sign-on</.docs_h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        Connecting an identity provider is a paid feature. <.plan_note tier={:team} />
      </p>
      <.docs_callout kind={:note} title="Provision the person before testing sign-in.">
        <p>
          Entra's v2 ID token does not include <.docs_inline_code>email_verified</.docs_inline_code>.
          emisar accepts that omission only when the token's
          <.docs_inline_code>oid</.docs_inline_code>
          matches an active member provisioned by this Entra connection. Complete directory sync
          below before testing the first sign-in.
        </p>
      </.docs_callout>
      <ol class="mt-8 space-y-10">
        <li class="flex gap-4">
          <span class="grid h-8 w-8 flex-none place-items-center rounded-full bg-brand-500/20 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-300">
            1
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
            <.docs_step_venue>emisar</.docs_step_venue>
            <p class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">Start the connection.</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5">
              Open
              <a
                href={~p"/app/sso/new"}
                class="font-medium text-brand-400 underline decoration-zinc-700 underline-offset-4 hover:text-brand-300"
              >Team → Single sign-on → Add provider</a>
              and choose <strong class="text-zinc-200">Microsoft Entra ID</strong>. Leave the page open: the
              callback URL on it is what Entra asks for next, and Entra's values come back here
              at the end.
            </p>
            <.docs_screenshot
              src="/images/docs/sso/entra-emisar-add-provider.webp"
              title="emisar · Add provider"
              caption="Picking the provider here tailors the rest of the form to it."
              alt="emisar's Add provider form with the Provider type select outlined in green and set to Microsoft Entra ID."
            />
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4">
          <span class="grid h-8 w-8 flex-none place-items-center rounded-full bg-brand-500/20 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-300">
            2
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
            <.docs_step_venue>Entra</.docs_step_venue>
            <p class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">Register the application.</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5">
              In the Microsoft Entra admin center go to <strong class="text-zinc-200">App registrations → New registration</strong>. Under
              <strong class="text-zinc-200">Redirect URI</strong>
              choose the <strong class="text-zinc-200">Web</strong>
              platform and enter emisar's callback:
            </p>
            <.docs_value label="Redirect URI" copy_text="https://emisar.dev/sign_in/sso/callback">
              https://emisar.dev/sign_in/sso/callback
            </.docs_value>

            <.docs_screenshot
              src="/images/docs/sso/entra-app-registration.webp"
              title="Microsoft Entra admin center · Register an application"
              caption="The platform must be set to Web — the URI beside it is ignored until it is, and the form refuses to register without it."
              alt="Entra's Register an application form with the name emisar, Supported account types set to Single tenant only, and the Redirect URI section outlined in green: its platform dropdown reads Web and the adjacent field holds https://emisar.dev/sign_in/sso/callback."
            />
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4">
          <span class="grid h-8 w-8 flex-none place-items-center rounded-full bg-brand-500/20 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-300">
            3
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
            <.docs_step_venue>Entra</.docs_step_venue>
            <p class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">Create a client secret.</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5">
              Open <strong class="text-zinc-200">Certificates &amp; secrets → New client secret</strong>. Copy the
              <strong class="text-zinc-200">Value</strong>
              column, not <strong class="text-zinc-200">Secret ID</strong>
              — the value is shown once and is unrecoverable afterwards.
            </p>

            <.docs_screenshot
              src="/images/docs/sso/entra-client-secret.webp"
              title="Microsoft Entra · Certificates &amp; secrets"
              caption="Press New client secret, then copy Value while it is shown. Secret ID is not the credential."
              alt="The emisar app's Certificates and secrets blade with New client secret outlined in green above one saved secret whose Value and Secret ID are masked."
            />
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4">
          <span class="grid h-8 w-8 flex-none place-items-center rounded-full bg-brand-500/20 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-300">
            4
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
            <.docs_step_venue>Entra</.docs_step_venue>
            <p class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">Copy the client and tenant IDs.</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5">
              The registration <strong class="text-zinc-200">Overview</strong> page contains two
              values. Use <strong class="text-zinc-200">Application (client) ID</strong> as the
              client ID. Use <strong class="text-zinc-200">Directory (tenant) ID</strong> in the
              issuer URL.
            </p>
            <.docs_screenshot
              src="/images/docs/sso/entra-app-overview.webp"
              title="Microsoft Entra · App registration overview"
              caption="Application (client) ID is emisar's Client ID. Directory (tenant) ID below it goes into the issuer."
              alt="The emisar app registration's Overview blade with Application (client) ID outlined in green, alongside Object ID, Directory (tenant) ID, client credentials showing one secret, and one web redirect URI."
            />
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4">
          <span class="grid h-8 w-8 flex-none place-items-center rounded-full bg-brand-500/20 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-300">
            5
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
            <.docs_step_venue>emisar</.docs_step_venue>
            <p class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">Paste them into the connection.</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5">
              Return to the connection from step 1. Use
              <strong class="text-zinc-200">Application (client) ID</strong>
              as the client ID. Use
              the secret from step 3. Build the issuer from your tenant ID.
            </p>
            <.docs_value
              label="Issuer URL"
              copy_text="https://login.microsoftonline.com/YOUR-TENANT-ID/v2.0"
            >
              https://login.microsoftonline.com/YOUR-TENANT-ID/v2.0
            </.docs_value>
            <p class="mt-4">
              The trailing
              <.docs_inline_code>/v2.0</.docs_inline_code>
              selects Entra's v2.0 endpoint. Without it, Entra returns v1.0 tokens. The identifier
              claim is already <.docs_inline_code>oid</.docs_inline_code>.
              Entra assigns a different
              <.docs_inline_code>sub</.docs_inline_code>
              to each application. The
              <.docs_inline_code>oid</.docs_inline_code>
              claim also matches the value directory sync sends. Save the connection. After
              directory sync below has provisioned the same person, select <strong class="text-zinc-200">Enabled</strong>, save again, and sign in.
            </p>
            <.docs_screenshot
              src="/images/docs/sso/entra-emisar-credentials.webp"
              title="emisar · Add provider"
              caption="The issuer carries your tenant ID and ends in /v2.0. The identifier claim is already oid."
              alt="emisar's OIDC connection fields with Issuer URL, Client ID and Client secret each outlined in green, the Issuer URL placeholder showing https://login.microsoftonline.com/YOUR-TENANT-ID/v2.0, and the Identifier claim reading oid — Microsoft Entra."
            />
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <.docs_h2 id="scim">Directory sync</.docs_h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        Directory sync makes Entra responsible for the member lifecycle, provisioning people and
        removing their access after offboarding. It also supplies the active identity record used
        to join Entra's
        <.docs_inline_code>oid</.docs_inline_code>
        claim to sign-in. <.plan_note tier={:enterprise} />
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        You need the connection's <strong class="text-zinc-200">SCIM base URL</strong>
        and <strong class="text-zinc-200">bearer token</strong>
        —
        <.link
          navigate={~p"/docs/scim#enable"}
          class="text-brand-300 underline decoration-brand-500/40 underline-offset-4 hover:text-brand-200"
        >enabling directory sync</.link>
        shows where both come from.
      </p>
      <ol class="mt-8 space-y-10">
        <li class="flex gap-4">
          <span class="grid h-8 w-8 flex-none place-items-center rounded-full bg-brand-500/20 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-300">
            1
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
            <.docs_step_venue>Entra</.docs_step_venue>
            <p class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">Create the enterprise application.</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5">
              Provisioning needs a separate object from the sign-in app registration. Go to <strong class="text-zinc-200">Enterprise applications → New application → Create your own application</strong>.
              Name it <.docs_inline_code>emisar</.docs_inline_code>. Choose <strong class="text-zinc-200">Integrate any other application you do not find in the gallery</strong>.
            </p>
            <.docs_screenshot
              src="/images/docs/sso/entra-create-enterprise-app.webp"
              title="Microsoft Entra · Browse App Gallery"
              caption="The gallery is for apps Microsoft already ships an integration for. emisar is not one, so it is created by hand."
              alt="Entra's Browse Microsoft Entra App Gallery blade with the Create your own application button outlined in green, above gallery tiles for Amazon Web Services, Google Cloud Platform, Oracle and SAP."
            />
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4">
          <span class="grid h-8 w-8 flex-none place-items-center rounded-full bg-brand-500/20 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-300">
            2
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
            <.docs_step_venue>Entra</.docs_step_venue>
            <p class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">Point it at emisar.</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5">
              On the new application's <strong class="text-zinc-200">Provisioning</strong>
              page, set <strong class="text-zinc-200">Provisioning Mode</strong>
              to <strong class="text-zinc-200">Automatic</strong>. Enter the SCIM base URL as <strong class="text-zinc-200">Tenant URL</strong>. Enter the bearer as <strong class="text-zinc-200">Secret Token</strong>.
            </p>
            <.docs_value label="Tenant URL" copy_text="https://emisar.dev/scim/v2">
              https://emisar.dev/scim/v2
            </.docs_value>

            <.docs_screenshot
              src="/images/docs/sso/entra-provisioning.webp"
              title="Microsoft Entra · Enterprise application provisioning"
              caption="After the live test, the Provisioning overview reported a completed incremental cycle with one group and two users."
              alt="The emisar directory sync enterprise application's Provisioning overview in Entra, with tenant-specific identifiers masked and Current cycle status: Incremental sync completed outlined in green above 100% completed, one group and two users."
            />
            <p class="mt-4">
              Press <strong class="text-zinc-200">Test Connection</strong>. Entra queries a random
              GUID that cannot exist. It expects an empty result, not an error. emisar returns that
              result. A failure means the URL or token is wrong, not the schema. Save.
            </p>

            <.docs_screenshot
              src="/images/docs/sso/entra-provisioning-credentials.webp"
              title="Microsoft Entra · Connectivity"
              caption="Leave authentication on Bearer. Tenant URL and the masked bearer sit together above Test connection."
              alt="The Connectivity page for the emisar directory sync enterprise application, with the connection form outlined in green: Bearer authentication selected, Tenant URL set to https://emisar.dev/scim/v2, Secret token masked, and Test connection beneath."
            />
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4">
          <span class="grid h-8 w-8 flex-none place-items-center rounded-full bg-brand-500/20 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-300">
            3
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
            <.docs_step_venue>Entra</.docs_step_venue>
            <p class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">Remap externalId to objectId.</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5">
              Open <strong class="text-zinc-200">Manage → Attribute mapping</strong>
              and change the source attribute feeding
              <.docs_inline_code>externalId</.docs_inline_code>
              from
              <.docs_inline_code>mailNickname</.docs_inline_code>
              to <.docs_inline_code>objectId</.docs_inline_code>. On a tenant
              still using Entra's older provisioning screens, the same setting lives under <strong class="text-zinc-200">Mappings → Provision Microsoft Entra ID Users</strong>.
            </p>

            <.docs_screenshot
              src="/images/docs/sso/entra-attribute-mapping.webp"
              title="Microsoft Entra · Attribute mapping"
              caption="The saved result: objectId now feeds externalId. Open this row to verify the complete mapping."
              alt="The emisar directory sync application's Attribute mapping list on the Users tab, with the row mapping objectId to externalId outlined in green among the surrounding user mappings."
            />

            <.docs_screenshot
              src="/images/docs/sso/entra-externalid-objectid.webp"
              title="Microsoft Entra · Edit Attribute Mapping"
              caption="Change the source, not the target — externalId must stay aligned with the OIDC oid claim."
              alt="Entra's Edit Attribute Mapping pane with the Source attribute row outlined in green and set to objectId, alongside Mapping type Direct, Target attribute externalId, and Apply this mapping set to Always."
            />
            <p class="mt-4">
              Entra defaults to <.docs_inline_code>mailNickname</.docs_inline_code>.
              This value can be missing, duplicated, or changed. It also differs from the identifier
              used by the sign-in connection. If SSO uses
              <.docs_inline_code>oid</.docs_inline_code>
              while SCIM uses <.docs_inline_code>mailNickname</.docs_inline_code>, one person
              becomes two identities. The directory provisions one, and sign-in creates another.
              <.docs_inline_code>objectId</.docs_inline_code>
              is the same
              immutable value as <.docs_inline_code>oid</.docs_inline_code>, so
              both flows identify one person.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4">
          <span class="grid h-8 w-8 flex-none place-items-center rounded-full bg-brand-500/20 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-300">
            4
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
            <.docs_step_venue>Entra</.docs_step_venue>
            <p class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">Assign the people to sync.</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5">
              Under <strong class="text-zinc-200">Users and groups</strong>, assign each person who
              needs an emisar account. Then, on <strong class="text-zinc-200">Provisioning → Settings</strong>, set
              <strong class="text-zinc-200">Scope</strong>
              to <strong class="text-zinc-200">Sync only assigned users and groups</strong>
              and turn <strong class="text-zinc-200">Provisioning Status</strong>
              on. Scope is separate from assignment and defaults to everyone. Change it, or Entra
              sends the entire directory regardless of assignment. Entra syncs roughly every 40
              minutes. New members appear under
              <strong class="text-zinc-200">Synced members</strong>
              after the next cycle, not immediately. Their Entra groups then appear under <strong class="text-zinc-200">Synced groups</strong>.
            </p>
            <.docs_screenshot
              src="/images/docs/sso/entra-assign-users.webp"
              title="Entra · Users and groups"
              caption="The certification group is assigned here and was provisioned to emisar."
              alt="The Users and groups page of the emisar SCIM enterprise application, with Add user/group visible and the assigned emisar certification members group outlined in green."
            />
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <p class="mt-8 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        <strong class="text-zinc-200">Next:</strong>
        configure
        <.link
          navigate={~p"/docs/scim#role-mapping"}
          class="text-brand-300 underline decoration-brand-500/40 underline-offset-4 hover:text-brand-200"
        >Role mapping</.link>
        so directory groups grant the right Emisar role.
      </p>
    </.docs_layout>
  </section>

  <.marketing_footer />
</div>
